+// --- Brick collision resolution (ISSUES.md #1) ------------------------------
+
+// Coarsest sub-step allowed when sweeping the ball's path. The ball is 14 px
+// across, so a sub-step under its diameter can never skip a brick (a brick is
+// only 20 px tall; crossing it top-to-bottom needs 34 px = BRICK_H + diameter,
+// against 35.5 px for a capped 50 ms frame at level 6). Staying at 2 px also
+// keeps face detection honest at seams: the 8 px grid gap lets the ball
+// straddle two bricks with at most 3 px of horizontal overlap, so a sub-step
+// below that still classifies a straight-down seam shot as a top hit.
